        }
      ],
      "extract": "The usual formulation of the powercounting in mesonic ChPT \\cite{Weinberg0} assumes that all the momenta in all diagrams are soft and this allows the powercounting to work as simple dimensional counting. In baryon and heavy meson ChPT one takes a step further. There is a line with a heavy mass running through all diagrams but in a way all spatial momenta can still be considered small. In vector meson ChPT it has",
      "extractCut": true
